Description: avfilter/tonemap_cuda: choose the reshaping piece by its index
 The reshape kernel chose a component's piece by blending the
 coefficients of neighbouring pieces with mix(x, y, t), which computes
 x + (y - x) * t. t is 0 or 1. With t = 1 the result can differ from y
 in the last bit. The kernel truncates the chosen piece's MMR offset to
 a whole row. So when a polynomial piece with a negative coefficient on
 s comes before an MMR piece, the blend can land just below that MMR
 piece's row, and the kernel reads the weights of the row before.
 .
 The release build compiles the kernel with clang and -ffast-math, and
 its output was right. Built without -ffast-math, on a synthetic profile
 5 picture whose P and T each have an MMR piece, a polynomial piece and
 another MMR piece, 272 of 663 checked patches came out more than one
 code from the definition, up to 498 luma codes.
 .
 Count the pivots that the signal reaches, and index the piece with that
 count, as tonemap_d3d11 does. With -ffast-math the output does not
 change.
